[2026-03-15T08:00:44.392Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9HaSUhgYx63KSHwDcacrG","type":"tool_result","content":"# replay-cli Reference\n\n**replay-cli** is a command-line tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports installation via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Recording**: Launch Replay Browser and capture sessions at specified URLs\n- **Authentication**: Use API keys from https://app.replay.io settings\n- **Management**: List, upload, and remove recordings locally\n- **Source Maps**: Upload source maps for workspace debugging\n\n## Essential Commands\n\nThe tool provides commands for:\n- `record [url]` - Start a recording session\n- `upload [ids...]` - Send recordings to Replay\n- `list` - View local recordings\n- `remove [ids...]` - Delete recordings\n- `login/logout` - Manage account access\n- `info` - Check CLI and browser versions\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally, set your `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable, then run `replayio record https://yourapp.com`. After recording, upload using the recording ID with the upload command.\n\nFor debugging recorded applications, you can integrate the Replay MCP Server with Claude using the provided configuration command."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c222c428-6363-4d7d-8b35-004fba3c5c4a","uuid":"c297369a-329d-48c6-9e55-b6ecbb3ccc9d","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# replay-cli Reference\n\n**replay-cli** is a command-line tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It supports installation via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Recording**: Launch Replay Browser and capture sessions at specified URLs\n- **Authentication**: Use API keys from https://app.replay.io settings\n- **Management**: List, upload, and remove recordings locally\n- **Source Maps**: Upload source maps for workspace debugging\n\n## Essential Commands\n\nThe tool provides commands for:\n- `record [url]` - Start a recording session\n- `upload [ids...]` - Send recordings to Replay\n- `list` - View local recordings\n- `remove [ids...]` - Delete recordings\n- `login/logout` - Manage account access\n- `info` - Check CLI and browser versions\n\n## Quick Start\n\nInstall globally, set your `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable, then run `replayio record https://yourapp.com`. After recording, upload using the recording ID with the upload command.\n\nFor debugging recorded applications, you can integrate the Replay MCP Server with Claude using the provided configuration command.","durationMs":3613,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T08:00:45.038Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UbqzKnuexudEQXUAG1PYUh","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As stated in the documentation: \"These recordings perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Investigation Approach\n\nThe recommended methodology involves four steps:\n1. Frame your investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form hypotheses supported by gathered data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection (finding files, reading code execution)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Point details revealing variable values and component state\n- Expression evaluation at specific execution moments\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as a comprehensive database. Two fundamental units are **Points** (individual execution moments) and **Elements** (DOM node references independent of time).\n\nThe documentation emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions and systematically gathering evidence before drawing conclusions about application behavior."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c222c428-6363-4d7d-8b35-004fba3c5c4a","uuid":"a2b10f2f-6401-4ce9-9978-fb91f5347055","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\n**Replay MCP** is a tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data. As stated in the documentation: \"These recordings perfectly capture everything that happened when a browser visited an app or other web page.\"\n\n## Key Investigation Approach\n\nThe recommended methodology involves four steps:\n1. Frame your investigation as a specific question\n2. Use exploratory tools to identify relevant events\n3. Apply explanatory tools to understand causation\n4. Form hypotheses supported by gathered data\n\n## Tool Categories\n\n**Exploratory Tools** discover what happened and when:\n- Error tracking (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection (finding files, reading code execution)\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Point details revealing variable values and component state\n- Expression evaluation at specific execution moments\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nThe recording functions as a comprehensive database. Two fundamental units are **Points** (individual execution moments) and **Elements** (DOM node references independent of time).\n\nThe documentation emphasizes avoiding premature conclusions and systematically gathering evidence before drawing conclusions about application behavior.","durationMs":3348,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
