[2026-03-15T08:01:02.970Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GEwcZcejhey3GeS5NWaLzP","type":"tool_result","content":"2-\n3-## Page: Search Page (Home)\n4-\n5-### Components\n6-- TripTypeSelector\n7:- PassengerCountSelector\n8-- CabinClassSelector\n9-- AirportAutocomplete\n10-- DatePicker\n11-- SearchButton\n12-- RecentSearches\n--\n54-- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n55-- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with default \"Round trip\"\n56-- **Action**: User selects \"One way\", then interacts with another element (e.g., clicks airport field), then opens the trip type selector again and selects \"Round trip\"\n57-- **Expected**: Each interaction correctly updates the selector. The dropdown opens and closes properly on each use. The final state shows \"Round trip\" selected.\n58-\n59:### PassengerCountSelector\n60-\n61:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector displays default \"1 Adult\"\n62:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n63-- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n64-- **Action**: User observes the passenger count selector\n65-- **Expected**: The selector displays \"1\" or \"1 Adult\" as the default.\n66-\n67:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector opens dropdown with passenger categories\n68:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n69-- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, passenger selector is closed\n70-- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count selector\n71-- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing three categories: Adults, Children, and Infants. Each category has a label, a current count, and \"+\" and \"−\" buttons.\n72-\n73:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments adult count\n74:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n75-- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n76-- **Action**: User clicks the \"+\" button next to Adults\n77-- **Expected**: Adults count increases to 2. The selector label updates to reflect the new total (e.g., \"2 passengers\" or \"2 Adults\").\n78-\n79:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector decrements adult count with minimum of 1\n80:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n81-- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n82-- **Action**: User clicks the \"−\" button next to Adults\n83-- **Expected**: Adults count remains at 1. The \"−\" button is disabled or has no effect since at least 1 adult is required.\n84-\n85:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements children\n86:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n87-- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Children count is 0\n88-- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Children twice, then clicks \"−\" once\n89-- **Expected**: Children count goes to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n90-\n91:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements infants\n92:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n93-- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Infants count is 0\n94-- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n95-- **Expected**: Infants count increases to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n96-\n97:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector prevents infants exceeding adults\n98:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n99-- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 1, Infants = 1\n100-- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n101-- **Expected**: Infants count remains at 1 (cannot exceed number of adults). The \"+\" button is disabled or has no effect.\n102-\n103:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector closes dropdown and retains values\n104:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n105-- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 2, Children = 1, Infants = 0\n106-- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown to close it\n107-- **Expected**: Dropdown closes. The selector label shows the updated total (e.g., \"3 passengers\"). Reopening the dropdown shows the same values (2 Adults, 1 Child, 0 Infants).\n108-\n109:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector can be used repeatedly\n110:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n111-- **Initial state**: Search page with default passenger counts\n112-- **Action**: User opens the selector, adds 1 adult, closes it, interacts with another element (e.g., selects cabin class), then reopens the passenger selector and adds 1 child\n113-- **Expected**: All values persist correctly between opens. Final state shows 2 Adults, 1 Child. The selector works correctly on each subsequent use.\n114-\n115-### CabinClassSelector\n--\n361-- **Initial state**: User has performed one search (LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 1 adult)\n362-- **Action**: User navigates back to the search page and observes recent searches\n363-- **Expected**: One recent search entry is displayed showing \"LAX → JFK\", the dates \"Mar 25 – Apr 1\", and \"1 passenger\".\n364-\n365-#### Test: RecentSearches clicking a recent search re-populates the form\n366:- **Components**: RecentSearches, AirportAutocomplete, DatePicker, PassengerCountSelector, TripTypeSelector, CabinClassSelector\n367-- **Initial state**: A recent search exists (LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 2 adults, Business class, Round trip)\n368-- **Action**: User clicks on the recent search entry\n369-- **Expected**: The search form is populated with the recent search parameters: origin = LAX, destination = JFK, departure = Mar 25, return = Apr 1, passengers = 2 adults, cabin class = Business, trip type = Round trip. The search is executed and the app navigates to the results page.\n370-\n371-#### Test: RecentSearches displays multiple recent searches in order\n--\n452-- **Initial state**: Results page showing round trip search with return Apr 1\n453-- **Action**: User clicks the return date parameter in the summary bar\n454-- **Expected**: A date picker opens with Apr 1 selected. User selects Apr 5. The search re-executes with the new return date and results update.\n455-\n456-#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit passengers\n457:- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, PassengerCountSelector\n458-- **Initial state**: Results page showing search with 1 adult\n459-- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count parameter in the summary bar\n460-- **Expected**: A passenger selector dropdown opens showing Adults: 1, Children: 0, Infants: 0. User increments adults to 2 and closes. The search re-executes with 2 adults and results update with new pricing.\n461-\n462-#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit cabin class"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c222c428-6363-4d7d-8b35-004fba3c5c4a","uuid":"3a1fb5ca-798a-4570-a0c0-398e41aadf18","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"2-\n3-## Page: Search Page (Home)\n4-\n5-### Components\n6-- TripTypeSelector\n7:- PassengerCountSelector\n8-- CabinClassSelector\n9-- AirportAutocomplete\n10-- DatePicker\n11-- SearchButton\n12-- RecentSearches\n--\n54-- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n55-- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with default \"Round trip\"\n56-- **Action**: User selects \"One way\", then interacts with another element (e.g., clicks airport field), then opens the trip type selector again and selects \"Round trip\"\n57-- **Expected**: Each interaction correctly updates the selector. The dropdown opens and closes properly on each use. The final state shows \"Round trip\" selected.\n58-\n59:### PassengerCountSelector\n60-\n61:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector displays default \"1 Adult\"\n62:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n63-- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n64-- **Action**: User observes the passenger count selector\n65-- **Expected**: The selector displays \"1\" or \"1 Adult\" as the default.\n66-\n67:#### Test: PassengerCountSelector opens dropdown with passenger categories\n68:- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n69-- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, passenger selector is closed\n70-- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count selector\n71-- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing three